    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: cauchy-schwarz-oq-02-oq-01\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nThis problem formalizes Parseval's identity for Fourier coefficients on the circle: the total squared Fourier coefficient mass equals the L² energy of the function. It extends cauchy-schwarz-oq-02 by applying L²/Pythagorean structure to orthonormal Fourier modes.\n\n## Local Proof Evidence\n\nThe current proof metadata for Proofs/CauchySchwarzOQ02OQ01.lean records 10 theorems, 0 sorries, and 0 axioms. The Lean source includes parseval_energy, parseval_hassum, bessel_fourier, Fourier orthonormality facts, fourier_pythagorean_partial, parseval_implies_completeness, and fourier_series_L2_convergence.\n\n## Next Directions\n\nLocal notes list the inner-product Parseval/Plancherel polarization form and an abstract Hilbert-basis version as follow-up extensions.\n"
